## 1 — Redux Thunk

Includes in `@reduxjs/toolkit`. Dispatch async functions. Best for simple, linear async flows.

```ts
export const fetchUser = createAsyncThunk(
  'user/fetch',
  async (id: string) => (await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`)).json(),
);
```

## 2 — Redux Saga

Uses generator functions and effect descriptors. Excellent for cancellation, retries, debounce, complex sequencing.

```ts
function* watchFetch() {
  yield takeLatest('user/fetch', fetchUserSaga);
}
```

## 3 — Redux Observable

Streams actions as RxJS Observables. Best when your team is experienced with RxJS.

```ts
const fetchUserEpic: Epic = (action$) =>
  action$.pipe(
    ofType('user/fetch'),
    switchMap((action) =>
      from(fetch(`/api/users/${action.payload}`).then((r) => r.json())).pipe(
        map(userLoaded),
        catchError(() => of(userFailed())),
      ),
    ),
  );
```

## 4 — RTK Query (recommended for data fetching)

Built into Redux Toolkit. Defines endpoints declaratively; generates hooks, caching, and invalidation automatically.

```ts
const api = createApi({
  reducerPath: 'api',
  baseQuery: fetchBaseQuery({ baseUrl: '/api' }),
  endpoints: (build) => ({
    getUser: build.query<User, string>({
      query: (id) => `users/${id}`,
    }),
  }),
});

// In component:
const { data, isLoading } = api.useGetUserQuery(userId);
```

## Choosing

| | Thunk | Saga | Observable | RTK Query |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Complexity | Low | High | High | Low |
| Cancellation | Manual | Built-in | Built-in | Built-in |
| Server state | Manual | Manual | Manual | First-class |
| Team prerequisite | None | Generator knowledge | RxJS knowledge | None |

